# SFR-write manifest — regenerated by audit_sfr_writes.py --update.
# Every entry: ADDR  PATTERN  IMMEDIATE  # source-file(s)
# Any diff between the current .rst set and this file fails the
# audit gate. Update ONLY after reviewing what changed and
# confirming the new write is intentional.
#
# Bug precedent — 2026-07-22 flash #2 was `USBCTL = 0xC0`
# (assign,0xc0) at 0xfffc when Rev 20 has (or,0x80). A baseline
# generated from a working image would have flagged that
# specific tuple as a diff before flash.
#
# NOTE: --update rewrites this file and DROPS per-entry annotations.
# Re-add the standing annotations below after any --update.
#
# RE-BASELINED 2026-07-28 (sixth time today), for sample byte order.
#   0xffd5 assign 0xac -> 0xa8  CPTRXCNF3 bit 2 is BYOR, the DMA byte-order
#     reversal for the capture path. Stock sets it and is documented as
#     S24_3BE; mboxfw declares S24_3LE, so it wants BYOR clear. Inferred
#     statically -- Linux quirks table + both stock images -- rather than
#     measured, which is why the first capture looked like full-scale
#     noise (correct audio, bytes in the other order).
#   0xffde (CPTCNF3) is now selected by MBOX_PLAYBACK_BYOR: 0xac (default,
#     stock boot value) or 0xa8. The manifest carries whichever the default
#     build emits; the two units run opposite settings to settle playback
#     byte order over a loopback cable.
#
# RE-BASELINED 2026-07-29, for the panel/EP0/suspend defect pass. Five new
# writes, each matching a stock site:
#   0xff6f runtime  IEPDCNTY0 = 0, and
#   0xffaf runtime  OEPDCNTY0 = 0 -- the EP0 Y-buffer counts, cleared in
#     usb_ep0_setup(). Rev 20 fcn.0x0970 @ 0x0988 / @ 0x0984; Rev 22
#     fcn.0x0891 @ 0x08A9 / @ 0x08A5. Defensive clears against boot-ROM
#     residue, not configuration -- neither firmware writes the Y BASE
#     registers. Candidate for the ~12% geometric EP0 IN loss.
#   0xffe1 and_not 0x3f  ACGCTL, idling both clock generators on suspend.
#     Rev 20 @ 0x0530, Rev 22 @ 0x052F. Inverse of the `or 0xc0` that
#     streaming.c already emits at Rev 20 0x07CC.
#   0xfffc and_not 0x7f  USBCTL, dropping CONN on resume before the
#     re-init tail. Rev 20 @ 0x054A, Rev 22 @ 0x0549.
#   0xfffd runtime  USBIMSK on resume. DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE: stock
#     assigns 0x9F here (Rev 20 @ 0x054E), which masks SUSR and RESR off
#     and makes suspend a one-shot per attach. We OR our own 0xF5 back
#     instead, so later suspends still work, and OR rather than assign per
#     task #48. See the comment in mboxfw/src/power.c.

